203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Day trading patterns are technical analysis tools used to identify potential trading opportunities within a single trading day. They are based on the analysis of price movements and can help traders identify possible trend reversals, continuations, or short-term price fluctuations.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
204 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Types of Day Trading Patterns You Should Know)
/E (Types of Day Trading Patterns You Should Know)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (There are two main ways to categorize chart patterns. The first is by the number of candlesticks it takes to form the pattern, and the other categorization is by the bias of the pattern.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Candlestick and Chart Patterns)
/E (Candlestick and Chart Patterns)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Going by the number of candlesticks, a pattern can be a candlestick or a chart pattern. A candlestick pattern takes only a few candlesticks to form. Anywhere from 1 candlestick to 4 candlesticks. These patterns are a result of the observation of each candle to decode a short-term market sentiment.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4 5]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Reversal and Continuation Patterns)
/E (Reversal and Continuation Patterns)
/Pg 9 0 R
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Going by its bias, a pattern can either be reversal or continuation. As the name suggests, reversal patterns indicate that a current is likely to reverse. So, if you were in a bullish trend and a reversal pattern appears, we are likely to see a reversal to a bearish trend. Traders use reversal patterns to predict the end of one trend and the beginning of another. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Continuation patterns, on the other hand, suggest that a current trend is likely to continue. Traders use these patterns to get into positions on established trends.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
