/ActualText (Very similar to the ascending and descending triangle patterns above is the symmetrical triangle pattern. The symmetrical triangle pattern is a trend continuation pattern that appears when the price briefly pauses its current trend before continuing. It is characterized by the confining of the price between two converging trendlines. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (If the symmetrical triangle pattern appears in a bullish trend, we will likely see a breakout to the upside and a continuation of the bullish trend. Conversely, if the pattern appears in a bearish trend, we will likely see a bearish continuation.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
