/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Although they are single candlestick patterns, they give a strong narrative of what the market is trying to do. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
338 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The hammer, for instance, is a bullish reversal pattern that appears after a downtrend. It appears on your chart as a candlestick with a long lower wick and a small body. The long lower wick suggests that there was strong selling pressure, but the small body indicates that buyers were able to push the price back up, implying a potential reversal.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
