/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Engulfing patterns are two-candle reversal patterns. The pattern forms when one candlestick is significantly bigger than the previous candlestick of the opposite bias. For instance, the bullish engulfing candlestick comprises a small bearish candlestick followed by a significantly larger bullish candlestick. Similarly, the bearish engulfing candlestick is formed by a small bullish candlestick followed by a strong and significantly larger bearish candle stick.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
